Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/044-skill-advisor-stress-ci (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)
Worktree: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/186-skill-advisor-stress-ci (your current directory)

ROLE: You fix three test files and reword one comment.

CONTEXT: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` default-exports `dualPlugin('system-skill-advisor', MkSkillAdvisorPlugin)`. That is a plain object `{ id, setup, server }`, and `server(input, options)` is the OpenCode 1 plugin function that returns hooks. Three runtime tests still call the default export itself as a function, so they fail with `TypeError: default is not a function` or `MkSkillAdvisorPlugin is not a function`:
- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/compiled-routing-consumption.vitest.ts` (import at line 16, calls at lines 62 and 83)
- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-graph-diagnostic-redaction.vitest.ts` (import at line 10, call at line 54)
- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts` (`const MkSkillAdvisorPlugin = skillAdvisorPlugin.default;` at line 24, calls at lines 137, 183 and 195)

ACTION:
1. In each of the three files, call the plugin through `.server(...)` on the default export with the same arguments. For the first two files, rename the default import to `skillAdvisorPlugin` and call `skillAdvisorPlugin.server(...)`. For `system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts`, change line 24 to bind the server function: `const MkSkillAdvisorPlugin = skillAdvisorPlugin.default.server;`. Leave its call sites as they are, unless TypeScript or the tests then need otherwise.
2. In `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/stress-test/skill-advisor/opencode-plugin-bridge-stress.vitest.ts`, replace the two comment lines above the test `keeps the dual-export object shape on the default export`. The new comment must say only what the test asserts: that the default export keeps the dual-export `id`, `setup` and `server` fields that both OpenCode versions load. It must not claim to catch a harness that calls the default directly, because the behavioural tests catch that.
Keep each file's existing style and indentation. Make no other edits, and don't put ids or paths in comments.

ALLOWED WRITE PATHS: the four files named above, and nothing else.

BANNED OPERATIONS: editing any other file; changing the plugin or v2-bridge; git commit, push, branch, stash or reset; installs; running opencode or opencode2; writing outside the worktree.

FORMAT: When done, reply with `git diff --stat` and one line per file saying what changed.
